      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "I think this looks great, thanks! I have a question about the implications of moving from Location/Window to Document, since these are not always 1:1.\r\n\r\nExample: you navigate an iframe from the initial about:blank Document to a same-origin one. I think neither the inner Window nor Location objects change, yet this PR would recalculate ancestor origins after the navigation, where as the current spec would not. Is that ever observable?\r\n\r\nI envisioned a case where an iframe's ancestor used `document.domain` to change its origin before the navigation away from the initial about:blank Document. The current spec would not reflect the ancestor's origin change, since ancestorOrigins never gets recalculated. After this PR, the new document's ancestor origins list gets recalculated to its ancestor's \"ancestor origins list\" _plus_ the ancestor's origin, which could have changed. On the other hand, we only ever expose its [ASCII serialization](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/C#ascii-serialisation-of-an-origin), which never considers an origin's domain, so I guess it's not observable.\r\n\r\nSo basically after this PR, in the navigation scenario I described above, the \"internal ancestor origins objects list\" CAN change, but not in a way that is observable to script. Is that right?\r\n\r\n**Edit**: Regarding the PR template, if there is indeed no observable change here, maybe the \"At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\" becomes \"N/A\"?\r\n\r\n<!-- I don't think the below is actually relevant:\r\n\r\nconst iframe = document.createElement('iframe');\r\ndocument.body.append(iframe);\r\n\r\nconst oldInnerWin = iframe.contentWindow;\r\nconst oldInnerDoc = iframe.contentDocument;\r\nconst oldInnerLocation = iframe.contentWindow.location;\r\n\r\nconst loadPromise = new Promise(resolve => iframe.onload = resolve);\r\niframe.src = \"https://example.com\";\r\nawait loadPromise;\r\n\r\nconst newInnerWin = iframe.contentWindow;\r\nconst newInnerDoc = iframe.contentDocument;\r\nconst newInnerLocation = iframe.contentWindow.location;\r\n\r\nconsole.assert(oldInnerWin === newInnerWin, 'Windows match');\r\nconsole.assert(oldInnerWin.location === newInnerWin.location, 'Location *getters* match');\r\nconsole.assert(oldInnerLocation === newInnerLocation, 'Cached Location objects match');\r\n-->",
    "state": "APPROVED",
